WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.099 --> 00:00:05.566
Professor Sycamore’s Pokémon summer camp

2
00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:09.133
is beginning its sixth day and our heroes have been battling

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.233
Tierno and his friends for entry into the summer camp hall of fame!

4
00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.833
With a rivalry both friendly and fierce,

5
00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:18.566
the two teams are currently tied for the lead

6
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:22.133
and to break that tie, it’s time for the final event,

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.000
the Team Battle Competition!

8
00:00:27.766 --> 00:00:30.166
Wingull! Gull, Gull, Gull! Wingull!

9
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.966
- Good morning, everyone!
- Good morning, Professor!

10
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.699
It’s already day six of camp,

11
00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:43.433
which means we finally decide who gets into the hall of fame!

12
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.966
So, get ready for the Team Battle Competition!

13
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.966
- Wow!
- That's awesome!

14
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.466
Wow! Yeah!

15
00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:56.000
- Team battle, huh?
- Pikachu!

16
00:00:56.066 --> 00:00:57.599
Everyone’s so excited.

17
00:00:57.666 --> 00:01:00.733
The Team Battle Competition works like a tournament.

18
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.133
As usual, the competing teams that take the top three spots will receive points.

19
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.200
We have two teams tied for the lead with 13 points

20
00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:11.133
and those teams are Team Froakie and Team Squirtle!

21
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.666
This is our final camp event, so give it all you’ve got and have fun!

22
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:17.133
Yeah!

23
00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:19.633
Pikachu!

24
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.700
A team battle consists of several Trainers forming a team

25
00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:25.633
and battling using various types of formations.

26
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.833
Now, today our team will be made up of three Trainers,

27
00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:32.066
but it can be a five or even a seven-person team!

28
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.366
- Wow, really?
- Pika.

29
00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:37.100
- It sounds confusing to me.
- Have you done this before, Clemont?

30
00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:39.866
Unfortunately, I’ve never had the chance.

31
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.066
- But it sounds like you guys have!
- That’s for sure.

32
00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:46.266
It usually happens whenever a lot of Trainers get together!

33
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:49.833
Yeah, she’s right. The next thing we usually do is have a strategy meeting.

34
00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:52.066
It’s fun to compare the personalities

35
00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:55.066
and skills of Pokémon while we decide on our formation.

36
00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.433
You come up with amazing Battle-combo moves!

37
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.566
It’s fun to put those Battle-combo moves to the test.

38
00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:03.133
All right, Serena and Clemont, we can’t lose!

39
00:02:03.199 --> 00:02:06.066
We’ll win this competition and get into the hall of fame!

40
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.933
Pika, Pika!

41
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.866
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

42
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:13.533
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

43
00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.100
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

44
00:02:17.166 --> 00:02:20.266
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

45
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:23.333
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

46
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.533
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

47
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

48
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

49
00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:34.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

50
00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:37.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

51
00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:52.400
Now, Pikachu, let’s get it going with Electro Ball!

52
00:02:52.466 --> 00:02:55.266
Pika! Pika, Pika, Pika, Chupi!

53
00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:59.266
Fennekin, use Hidden Power! Combine it with that Electro Ball!

54
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.333
Fenn!

55
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.066
All right, Bunnelby, Dig!

56
00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.100
Bunnelby!

57
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:05.466
Fenn!

58
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.466
- It worked!
- Awesome, Serena!

59
00:03:08.533 --> 00:03:11.266
- That Battle-combo move was cool!
- Yeah.

60
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:13.500
Serena could be a great performer, no doubt!

61
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:26.000
Marvelous! Team Froakie has now made it through this battle

62
00:03:26.066 --> 00:03:28.033
and that means on to the finals!

63
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.266
- All right!
- Fenn!

64
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:32.533
- Pikachu!
- Bunnel!

65
00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.433
It’s time for the final battle against Team Squirtle,

66
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.033
who has already moved to the finals!

67
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.100
- Yeah, they did it!
- Dedenne!

68
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:42.100
I knew Team Froakie would get here!

69
00:03:42.166 --> 00:03:45.266
I can see why everyone likes team battling so much!

70
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.500
- It’s exciting!
- Sure is!

71
00:03:47.566 --> 00:03:50.733
I’ve got to agree it’s a lot of fun!

72
00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:55.799
And now, before we get under way, both teams will have their strategy meetings.

73
00:03:57.899 --> 00:04:01.100
- Won’t be long now.
- Time to put our plan into high gear.

74
00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:03.066
Making it real for the steal!

75
00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.299
So here’s our plan.

76
00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:12.866
- Wobbuffet!
- Will you calm down? Not yet!

77
00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:15.600
This time I’ve come up with a savory strategy

78
00:04:15.666 --> 00:04:18.566
as luscious as a well-seasoned slow-cooked stew!

79
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:21.166
If we get our hands on Squirtle and the others,

80
00:04:21.233 --> 00:04:23.533
Pikachu will surely come running to save them.

81
00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:26.066
And if we use Squirtle and its buddies as shields,

82
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.333
Pikachu won’t be able to lay a paw on us.

83
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.466
We’ll grab the load of them without a fight!

84
00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:32.000
Attention!

85
00:04:32.066 --> 00:04:35.900
I’d like you all to get started on today’s menu, please.

86
00:04:35.966 --> 00:04:38.666
- And thank you!
- Yes, ma’am!

87
00:04:38.733 --> 00:04:41.400
Our first-class cuisine must come to an end.

88
00:04:41.466 --> 00:04:43.099
Parting is such sweet sorrow.

89
00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:45.633
‘Cause we’re going back to our regular gig, dig?

90
00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.733
Wobbuffet!

91
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.166
Hello there, Trainers!

92
00:04:50.233 --> 00:04:52.233
All right! It’s the camp cooks.

93
00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.733
Kudos for making it to the final round!

94
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.300
How nice! Thanks a lot!

95
00:04:56.366 --> 00:04:59.166
We owe you a lot for always making such yummy food.

96
00:04:59.233 --> 00:05:01.300
Oh, you’ve made me a happy chef!

97
00:05:01.366 --> 00:05:04.366
- Is there something we can do for you?
- There is!

98
00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:06.766
Before the finals, we thought we’d give your Pokémon

99
00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:08.300
a complimentary health checkup!

100
00:05:08.366 --> 00:05:11.033
But wouldn’t the Pokémon Center be the place to do that?

101
00:05:11.099 --> 00:05:12.966
Nurse Joy’s busy with the twerps...

102
00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:16.266
What I mean to say is she’s busy with Pikachu and all the others!

103
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.066
We may look like just chefs.

104
00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:20.266
But we’re licensed healthcare workers, too.

105
00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:21.466
You are?

106
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:24.333
Having healthcare professionals who can cook is awesome!

107
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.866
Sure is. All right!

108
00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:28.500
I think you’ve said enough.

109
00:05:28.566 --> 00:05:30.200
Okay, then, thanks!

110
00:05:30.266 --> 00:05:32.400
Your Pokémon, if you please.

111
00:05:32.466 --> 00:05:35.466
- See you later, Squirtle.
- You too, Charmander.

112
00:05:35.533 --> 00:05:39.966
- We’ll treat them like they were ours.
- Off to the Pokémon Center!

113
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.200
Okay, here you go!

114
00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:50.966
- Picapi! Pikachu!
- Buddy!

115
00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.733
We’re all finished. Everybody’s healthy.

116
00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.099
That’s great. Thanks a lot, Nurse Joy.

117
00:05:56.166 --> 00:05:59.966
- And now it’s time for the final battle!
- Yay! I’m so excited!

118
00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:02.599
-Nurse Joy!

119
00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:05.099
- Huh?
- We’re here for our Pokémon!

120
00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:09.000
- Huh? That’s confusing. Uh...
- Wigglytuff!

121
00:06:09.066 --> 00:06:13.599
- I’m afraid they’re not here.
- Huh?

122
00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.166
Ready or not, it’s checkup time!

123
00:06:24.233 --> 00:06:25.333
- Squirtle!
- Char!

124
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.833
- Pumpkaboo!
- Pumpkaboo!

125
00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.799
Leech Seed, let’s go!

126
00:06:30.866 --> 00:06:32.466
Boo!

127
00:06:36.166 --> 00:06:39.666
Stay calm. The best thing you can do for yourselves now is relax.

128
00:06:39.733 --> 00:06:43.099
A chilled Pokémon is a happy Pokémon.

129
00:06:43.166 --> 00:06:46.299
- Our chefs did that?
- Pika?

130
00:06:46.366 --> 00:06:48.833
Hm. Guess they can do anything.

131
00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.833
They might still be busy with the checkup.

132
00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:53.066
Yeah, but it’s been such a long time.

133
00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:56.799
I think we should split up and go look for them!

134
00:07:01.533 --> 00:07:04.066
- Huh?
- Bunnelby!

135
00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:06.500
Hey, Bunnelby’s pointing over there.

136
00:07:08.433 --> 00:07:09.866
What is it, Fennekin?

137
00:07:09.933 --> 00:07:11.700
- Fenn!
- Bunn!

138
00:07:11.766 --> 00:07:13.200
- Fennekin!
- Bunnelby!

139
00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:14.466
- Pika!
- Pikachu!

140
00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:17.666
They all sense something. Quick, let’s follow them!

141
00:07:20.266 --> 00:07:21.466
Pik, Pik, Pik!

142
00:07:21.533 --> 00:07:24.066
- Hello! Chefs?
- Oh!

143
00:07:24.133 --> 00:07:26.700
Boss alert! Return!

144
00:07:26.766 --> 00:07:28.966
Cover up!

145
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.466
Oh, there you are! I was looking all over for you.

146
00:07:33.533 --> 00:07:37.200
Forgive us. We’re looking for vegetables for the kids.

147
00:07:37.266 --> 00:07:39.866
- Kin!
- Uh-oh?

148
00:07:39.933 --> 00:07:41.933
What’s this?

149
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.166
Fennekin!

150
00:07:44.233 --> 00:07:45.633
Where are the Pokémon?

151
00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.700
- Well, well.
- No need to grouse.

152
00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:49.933
Pikachu in the house!

153
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.099
Who’s that Pokémon?

154
00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.833
It’s Meowth!

155
00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.866
That's right!

156
00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:05.799
Fennekin?

157
00:08:06.799 --> 00:08:09.933
Oh Trespasser! Get away now!

158
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.833
- Your nose is getting out of joint!
- Bunnelby!

159
00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.733
- Is there something in there?
- Bunn!

160
00:08:14.799 --> 00:08:17.500
Fenn, Fenn! Kin! Kin!

161
00:08:17.566 --> 00:08:19.733
What have you done with all of our Pokémon?

162
00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.233
Char!

163
00:08:21.299 --> 00:08:24.733
Hey, cut it out! Leave our veggies alone!

164
00:08:24.799 --> 00:08:26.466
What is going on, Fennekin?

165
00:08:26.533 --> 00:08:28.733
Oh dear! Something’s got to be wrong!

166
00:08:28.799 --> 00:08:32.033
Both Fennekin and Bunnelby are sure something else is in there!

167
00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.533
Pika! Pikachu!

168
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.766
Now you’re just making things up!

169
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:37.733
Nothing in here but fresh veggies.

170
00:08:37.799 --> 00:08:41.166
And if you keep messing with us, there won’t be any veggies tonight!

171
00:08:41.233 --> 00:08:42.900
Pika!

172
00:08:42.966 --> 00:08:44.833
Pikachu!

173
00:08:46.233 --> 00:08:47.566
Huh?

174
00:08:47.633 --> 00:08:49.333
- Oh!
- Bulbasaur!

175
00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.766
- Squirtle!
- Charmander!

176
00:08:50.833 --> 00:08:53.300
Those are Pokémon and no matter what you say,

177
00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:55.000
they’re definitely not vegetables!

178
00:08:55.066 --> 00:08:57.733
What do you think you’re doing with them?

179
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.733
Prepare for trouble, we don’t think, we know

180
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.000
And make it a multi-kidnapping show.

181
00:09:04.066 --> 00:09:06.500
To protect the world from devastation!

182
00:09:06.566 --> 00:09:09.300
To unite all people within our nation!

183
00:09:09.366 --> 00:09:12.566
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

184
00:09:12.633 --> 00:09:15.933
To extend our reach to the stars above!

185
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.300
- Jessie!
- And James!

186
00:09:18.366 --> 00:09:21.066
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

187
00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:24.199
Surrender now or prepare for a frantic food fight!!

188
00:09:24.266 --> 00:09:27.400
- Meowth, that’s right!
- Wobbuffet!

189
00:09:29.366 --> 00:09:32.733
- Team Rocket! Not you again!
- Team Rocket?

190
00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.500
They’re bad guys who try to steal people’s Pokémon!

191
00:09:35.566 --> 00:09:37.900
Does that mean you’re not real chefs?

192
00:09:37.966 --> 00:09:40.333
I’m sorry, ma’am, but this is our day job.

193
00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.400
But you don’t have to pay us for today.

194
00:09:42.466 --> 00:09:44.800
These are the tools of the Team Rocket trade!

195
00:09:44.866 --> 00:09:46.566
- What did you say?
- No way!

196
00:09:46.633 --> 00:09:48.600
And now we go into act two!

197
00:09:51.866 --> 00:09:54.400
- Inkay!
- Pumkaboo!

198
00:09:54.466 --> 00:09:56.466
Don’t move a twerpish inch!

199
00:09:56.533 --> 00:09:59.766
Not if you wanna keep these lugs safe!

200
00:09:59.833 --> 00:10:03.199
- You cowards!
- Well, duh, we’re bad guys!

201
00:10:03.266 --> 00:10:06.100
If you want to save your friends, Pikachu, let’s make a deal.

202
00:10:06.166 --> 00:10:08.699
Join up with Team Rocket, we keep it real!

203
00:10:08.766 --> 00:10:11.300
- Wobb! Wobbu! Wobb!
- Pika!

204
00:10:11.366 --> 00:10:14.500
- That’s got to be a joke!
- Bulbasaur, hang in there!

205
00:10:14.566 --> 00:10:18.133
- Charmander, use Flamethrower!
- You’ve got to rip that vine apart!

206
00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:23.633
- We’ve got to get them out!
- Hm.

207
00:10:23.699 --> 00:10:28.033
Aw, what will you do? They all look rather sleepy to me.

208
00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.033
- Okay, Pikachu. Over here right now!
- Pikachu!

209
00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.033
We’ll get everyone out of there safely, no doubt!

210
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.433
Go, Bunnelby!

211
00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.900
Bunn!

212
00:10:37.966 --> 00:10:40.100
- Okay, Ash, now!
- Right!

213
00:10:40.166 --> 00:10:43.933
- Froakie, go!
- Froakie!

214
00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.699
- Fennekin, you too!
- Kin, Kin, Kin!

215
00:10:47.933 --> 00:10:49.400
Okay, Inkay, Psybeam!

216
00:10:49.466 --> 00:10:51.466
Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball!

217
00:10:51.533 --> 00:10:55.600
- Quick, Froakie, use your Frubbles, now!
- Froakie!

218
00:10:56.966 --> 00:10:58.900
Use Scratch, Fennekin!

219
00:10:58.966 --> 00:11:02.366
Fenn! Kin!

220
00:11:02.433 --> 00:11:05.833
- All right, Froakie, use Cut!
- Kin!

221
00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.733
Now, Pikachu, wrap it up with Thunderbolt!

222
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.800
Pika! Pikachu!

223
00:11:17.133 --> 00:11:19.133
We were really on a roll.

224
00:11:19.199 --> 00:11:21.966
At least cooking brought us in some extra funds.

225
00:11:22.033 --> 00:11:25.600
- Too bad we didn’t bring them!
- Wobbuff!

226
00:11:25.666 --> 00:11:28.366
We’re blasting off again!

227
00:11:28.433 --> 00:11:30.900
- Wobbuffet!
- Pumka!

228
00:11:32.699 --> 00:11:37.699
Oh, what a crying shame. And to think they were such talented chefs.

229
00:11:38.666 --> 00:11:41.533
- Glad you’re okay!
- Thanks to all of you.

230
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:45.266
- We owe you so very much!
- And now it’s time for the finals.

231
00:11:45.333 --> 00:11:47.333
This is going to be fun!

232
00:11:50.699 --> 00:11:54.333
Now, teams, are you all ready for our final battle?

233
00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.800
On my whistle, let's go!

234
00:12:00.433 --> 00:12:02.800
Pikachu!

235
00:12:02.866 --> 00:12:04.833
Char!

236
00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.366
- Here we come. Use Quick Attack!
- Pika!

237
00:12:07.433 --> 00:12:10.833
Not so fast! Charmander, use Flamethrower!

238
00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:11.900
Mander!

239
00:12:11.966 --> 00:12:16.133
All right, Fennekin, protect Pikachu with Flamethrower!

240
00:12:16.199 --> 00:12:20.333
- Fenn!
- Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik!

241
00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.533
- Use Rapid Spin on Pikachu, go!
- Squirt!

242
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.166
Pika!

243
00:12:26.433 --> 00:12:28.400
Now, use Water Gun on Fennekin!

244
00:12:28.466 --> 00:12:30.466
Squirtle! Squirtle!

245
00:12:30.533 --> 00:12:31.600
Fenn!

246
00:12:31.666 --> 00:12:34.233
They don’t waste a step. Squirtle can move!

247
00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.900
Now, Chespin, use Vine Whip on Squirtle!

248
00:12:36.966 --> 00:12:38.000
Chespin!

249
00:12:38.066 --> 00:12:40.866
- Dodge that!
- Squirt!

250
00:12:40.933 --> 00:12:43.500
Use Flame Burst on Chespin!

251
00:12:43.566 --> 00:12:45.533
Charmand!

252
00:12:45.599 --> 00:12:46.733
- Ches!
- Pika!

253
00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.633
- Pik!
- Pikachu?

254
00:12:48.699 --> 00:12:51.233
You just saw Flame Burst’s additional effect!

255
00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:54.333
You see, Flame Burst can cause damage to multiple targets!

256
00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.099
- Now, Razor Leaf!
- Bulbasaur!

257
00:12:57.166 --> 00:12:59.433
- Pika!
- Huh?

258
00:13:01.466 --> 00:13:04.633
- They’re trying to finish this.
- They’re really strong!

259
00:13:04.699 --> 00:13:07.033
- Squirt!
- Look at Squirtle’s rhythmic dancing.

260
00:13:07.099 --> 00:13:09.433
Just like it did before!

261
00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:13.166
- They’re using it to mount their attack.
- Rhythm.

262
00:13:13.233 --> 00:13:14.900
Man, are they good at that.

263
00:13:14.966 --> 00:13:18.699
Looks like Squirtle’s steps have them not knowing what to do next.

264
00:13:18.766 --> 00:13:21.433
It’s all in the moves. What can they do?

265
00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.833
We’ve got to break their rhythm. But how?

266
00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:32.366
- Bulbasaur, stand by for Solar Beam!
- Saur!

267
00:13:32.433 --> 00:13:34.666
We’ve got to do something to buy a little time

268
00:13:34.733 --> 00:13:36.533
until that Solar Beam’s all charged up!

269
00:13:36.599 --> 00:13:39.866
Well, all right, Squirtle! Aqua Tail on Fennekin, let’s rock!

270
00:13:39.933 --> 00:13:43.066
Squirt!

271
00:13:43.133 --> 00:13:47.599
- Fennekin, use Hidden Power!
- Fenn! Kin!

272
00:13:47.666 --> 00:13:48.833
Fenn!

273
00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.300
- Oh, Fennekin!
- Fenn.

274
00:13:51.366 --> 00:13:55.266
- Fennekin’s unable to battle!
- Fennekin, return!

275
00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:58.233
Now, Charmander, Flamethrower!

276
00:13:58.300 --> 00:13:59.800
- Dodge it, Pikachu!
- Pika!

277
00:13:59.866 --> 00:14:02.833
We’re all charged up! Use Solar Beam!

278
00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.333
- Pikachu, dodge it!
- Pik Pika!

279
00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.000
- Now Chespin, Vine Whip!
- Chespin!

280
00:14:13.666 --> 00:14:14.900
Pika, Pika!

281
00:14:14.966 --> 00:14:17.433
-That was some combination!

282
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.033
I thought we had a direct hit!

283
00:14:19.099 --> 00:14:21.766
Pikachu! Thunderbolt on Charmander!

284
00:14:21.833 --> 00:14:25.099
Pikachu!

285
00:14:25.166 --> 00:14:26.400
Char!

286
00:14:26.466 --> 00:14:28.099
Charmander is unable to battle!

287
00:14:28.166 --> 00:14:30.466
Okay, return.

288
00:14:31.699 --> 00:14:34.099
Thanks, Charmander! Get a good rest.

289
00:14:34.166 --> 00:14:36.566
Don’t worry. I’ll get them back for you!

290
00:14:36.633 --> 00:14:40.133
- Use Rapid Spin!
- Squirrrr!

291
00:14:40.199 --> 00:14:42.966
Ash, now it’s time for us to wrap this thing up!

292
00:14:43.033 --> 00:14:45.133
- Use Vine Whip!
- Chespin!

293
00:14:45.199 --> 00:14:48.533
Yeah, all right! Pikachu! Use Electro Ball!

294
00:14:48.599 --> 00:14:50.900
Pika! Pika, Pika, Pika, Pika Chupik!

295
00:14:50.966 --> 00:14:54.000
- Squirtle, dodge it, quick!
- Squirtle!

296
00:14:55.233 --> 00:14:56.366
Bulba!

297
00:14:56.433 --> 00:14:59.733
- Bulbasaur!
- Saur.

298
00:15:01.666 --> 00:15:04.666
- Chespin!
- Pika!

299
00:15:04.733 --> 00:15:07.866
Nice combination, guys, but we’re not done!

300
00:15:07.933 --> 00:15:11.199
- Aqua Tail!
- Squirt!

301
00:15:11.266 --> 00:15:12.300
Pika!

302
00:15:12.366 --> 00:15:17.866
- Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

303
00:15:21.833 --> 00:15:23.099
Oh.

304
00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.599
And that's the end of it

305
00:15:26.666 --> 00:15:28.966
Team Froakie is our winning team!

306
00:15:29.033 --> 00:15:31.900
And that means you’ll be in the hall of fame!

307
00:15:31.966 --> 00:15:34.900
-Congratulations to Team Froakie!

308
00:15:34.966 --> 00:15:38.566
Now, let’s give a big round of applause to our runners up,

309
00:15:38.633 --> 00:15:40.199
Team Squirtle!

310
00:15:43.699 --> 00:15:47.533
-Hall of fame! Hall of fame!

311
00:15:47.599 --> 00:15:52.000
- We did it. Yay!
- Oh, yeah, but Fennekin...

312
00:15:52.066 --> 00:15:55.199
Don’t worry, Serena! Fennekin may have lost today,

313
00:15:55.266 --> 00:15:57.566
but you can always use that to get stronger!

314
00:15:57.633 --> 00:15:59.933
- Pikachu!
- Chespin!

315
00:16:00.066 --> 00:16:02.666
Fenn!

316
00:16:04.266 --> 00:16:07.933
Ow! You were so awesome, Squirtle.

317
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.333
Squirt!

318
00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.300
Don’t worry, Squirtle. It’s okay to cry!

319
00:16:12.366 --> 00:16:17.066
- Nice battling, Bulbasaur.
- Bulb! Bulbasaur!

320
00:16:17.133 --> 00:16:20.533
We’ll get you back next time! Okay, Ash?

321
00:16:20.599 --> 00:16:23.599
- Okay!
- Pika! Pikachu!

322
00:16:26.266 --> 00:16:31.099
We’ve got a great surprise for you on our summer camp’s final night!

323
00:16:31.166 --> 00:16:36.466
These fireworks will help us celebrate our week of memories. Marvelous!

324
00:16:59.366 --> 00:17:01.966
- Hey, Tierno?
- Hm?

325
00:17:02.033 --> 00:17:06.399
Thinking about our last battle, can you show me your battle style again?

326
00:17:06.466 --> 00:17:07.466
Squirtle!

327
00:17:07.533 --> 00:17:09.966
You mean the way it moves and grooves?

328
00:17:10.033 --> 00:17:14.133
Uh-huh. I’ve never seen a battling style like that before.

329
00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:18.599
If we can learn how to battle like that, I think we’ll be a lot stronger.

330
00:17:18.666 --> 00:17:20.333
No doubt!

331
00:17:23.233 --> 00:17:25.933
See, I’m going to be challenging the Shalour Gym.

332
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.933
I’m sure your battling style would be really effective

333
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.433
at a Fighting-type Gym like Shalour.

334
00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.866
- A Gym battle. I get it. Yeah!
- Why don’t you show him?

335
00:17:33.933 --> 00:17:36.433
Moving and grooving like you do in battle is so cool!

336
00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:41.033
Not to mention a rhythmic battling style like that is really one of a kind.

337
00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.133
As far as I can see, by doing those dance steps and constantly moving around,

338
00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:48.200
it creates such smooth transitions between attacking and dodging!

339
00:17:48.266 --> 00:17:51.200
That’s right! See, it started out when I was thinking about

340
00:17:51.266 --> 00:17:54.033
how to make moves flow better when a Pokémon uses them

341
00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:55.933
and I came up with this way to do it.

342
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.533
Squirtle, Squirtle, Squirtle, Squirtle.

343
00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:01.366
Incorporating dance steps in our battle lets us read our opponent’s movements

344
00:18:01.433 --> 00:18:04.500
and makes it easier for us to make them battle at our pace.

345
00:18:04.566 --> 00:18:06.800
Oh, wow! Awesome!

346
00:18:06.866 --> 00:18:10.600
And to tell the truth, I had Tierno teach me some dance moves as well.

347
00:18:10.666 --> 00:18:12.800
I’m trying to use it as part of my performance.

348
00:18:12.866 --> 00:18:15.933
- You’re kidding me!
- That’s so cool! I want to see!

349
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.133
Okay, Ash. I’ll teach you how to move and groove.

350
00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.966
Thanks a lot, Tierno!

351
00:18:22.033 --> 00:18:24.700
Okay, everybody. Come on out!

352
00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.466
- Froak!
- Cha!

353
00:18:28.533 --> 00:18:31.233
- You’ve got to move it, too.
- What do you mean me?

354
00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:36.000
Yeah, you! The most important thing is for Trainer and Pokémon to become one.

355
00:18:36.066 --> 00:18:38.733
It won’t work unless you’re moving and grooving together.

356
00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:41.266
- I guess.
- Pika!

357
00:18:41.333 --> 00:18:43.833
- Pika, Pika!
- Squirt! Squirt, Squirt!

358
00:18:43.899 --> 00:18:46.566
Ha, yeah! Ready to rock!

359
00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.566
First, the basics, okay?

360
00:18:59.466 --> 00:19:01.700
Wingull! Wingull!

361
00:19:01.766 --> 00:19:05.266
Campers! I hereby announce that the official closing

362
00:19:05.333 --> 00:19:08.366
of this season’s Pokémon summer camp is upon us!

363
00:19:08.433 --> 00:19:11.800
Everyone, give yourselves a round of applause!

364
00:19:14.666 --> 00:19:17.833
I sincerely hope from the bottom of my heart that

365
00:19:17.899 --> 00:19:21.733
the experience all of you gained as you competed alongside your Pokémon

366
00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.666
will be truly memorable, as well as invaluable!

367
00:19:24.733 --> 00:19:27.033
May your journeys be rich and full

368
00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.666
and keep traveling onward and upward along with your Pokémon!

369
00:19:33.399 --> 00:19:37.166
Hey, Ash! Make sure you work on everything I showed you last night!

370
00:19:37.233 --> 00:19:38.600
You bet!

371
00:19:38.666 --> 00:19:41.666
I hope you follow through. I’m a little worried.

372
00:19:41.733 --> 00:19:44.166
Come on. I’ll be just fine!

373
00:19:44.233 --> 00:19:46.166
I guess it’s time to go.

374
00:19:46.233 --> 00:19:50.666
Yeah, you’re right, though it’s never easy to say goodbye.

375
00:19:53.733 --> 00:19:56.166
Serena, see you at the Pokétacular!

376
00:19:56.233 --> 00:19:58.666
- Okay!
- See you then!

377
00:20:04.133 --> 00:20:06.666
- Of course we’re all rivals now.
- For sure!

378
00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.800
Later! Take care!

379
00:20:14.866 --> 00:20:18.433
- Let’s battle again soon!
- Pika! Pika!

380
00:20:19.666 --> 00:20:22.033
And so, the curtain comes down

381
00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.800
on Professor Sycamore’s Pokémon summer camp,

382
00:20:24.866 --> 00:20:27.433
where Trainers and their Pokémon strengthened their bonds

383
00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.800
by competing and interacting with others.

384
00:20:29.866 --> 00:20:32.966
Will Ash be able to use Tierno’s unique battling style

385
00:20:33.033 --> 00:20:35.633
to help him win his Gym battle against Korrina?

386
00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:39.166
The answer to come, as the journey continues!
